Source: pg-local-cache
Section: database
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Ruohang Feng <rh@vonng.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), postgresql-all (>= 217~), libssl-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Rules-Requires-Root: no
Homepage: https://github.com/profundium/pg_local_cache

Package: postgresql-PGVERSION-pg-local-cache
Architecture: any
Provides: postgresql-pg-local-cache
Depends: ${postgresql:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Transaction-aware primary-key row cache for PostgreSQL PGVERSION
 pg_local_cache keeps bounded whole-row entries in PostgreSQL shared memory.
 Rows are served over authenticated RESP (Redis protocol) by a background
 worker; there is no SQL read fast path. It targets one configured database
 and one writable primary. The module must be added to shared_preload_libraries
 and PostgreSQL restarted before its cache workers can be used.
